    {
      "text": "Why did you choose to study that subject?",
      "speaker": "a",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.93
    },
    {
      "text": "Two reasons, really. One, in China everybody thinks computer science leads to a high-paid job — that's part of it. And two, I like computers. Fun fact: I was actually a chemistry student when I was a freshman, and then I switched to computer science. I chose it because I use computers every day, and I wanted to become a better user of them. So that's why — plus the high-paid job thing.",
      "speaker": "b",
      "start": 2.47,
      "end": 24.01
    }
